.Dd May 29, 2026
.Dt AGENT-GUIDE 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm agent-guide
.Nd live service and usage guide for AI agent sessions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
probes the local AI server, OTel collector, Grafana, Colima, and selected
tooling, then prints connection details and safe usage guidance for agents.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -json
Emit a JSON object.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_AI_ENDPOINT
.It Ev ZDOTDIR
Repository root.
.It Ev ZDOTS_AI_ENDPOINT
AI server base URL.
.It Ev ZDOTS_AI_MODE
AI operating mode.
.It Ev ZDOTS_LOG_DIR
Deploy log directory.
.El
.Sh FILESYSTEM DOCTRINE
Before any destructive filesystem operation, apply the Idiot Test:
"would an idiot do this?" If yes, stop and confirm with the user.
The 2026-05-25 incident (an agent ran
.Ic rm -rf ~/
after conflating a literal
.Pa ~
subdirectory with HOME expansion) caused permanent loss of shell config,
history,
.Pa ~/.config/ ,
and
.Pa ~/context/work/
research.
The
.Pa conf.d/15-safe-rm.zsh
wrapper is a backstop only \(em it does not fire in subshells, bash scripts,
or IDE-spawned shells.
Think first: resolve paths to absolute strings, echo and read the targets,
and prefer reversible operations
.Pq Ic del , Ic mv , Ic git rm
over
.Ic rm -rf .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr capabilities 1 ,
.Xr zdots-ctl 8 ,
.Xr zdots 7
